WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.130
Diamond is very hard, and it melts
only at a very high temperature.

2
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:08.250
Graphite is soft enough
to rub off onto paper.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.150
Both are pure carbon.

4
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.550
Yet wire them into a circuit, and
only graphite lets a current through.

5
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.110
Same element, opposite results.

6
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.970
Why does only graphite
conduct electricity?

7
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.950
In this mission, you'll explore
giant covalent networks:

8
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.510
diamond, graphite, graphene,
silicon and silicon dioxide.

9
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.670
You'll meet the fullerenes,
compare silicon with diamond,

10
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.510
and learn to predict a substance's
properties from its structure.

11
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.810
Your mission: explain why graphite
conducts but diamond doesn't.
